<title>DUBAI: GOLF-BJORN OUT OF DESERT CLASSIC.</title>
<headline>GOLF-BJORN OUT OF DESERT CLASSIC.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish golfer Thomas Bjorn, the European Tour rookie of the year for 1996, withdrew from the Desert Classic before the second round on Friday.</p>
<p>Bjorn, winner of the Loch Lomond Invitational in Scotland last year, pulled out because of a recurrence of a neck injury.</p>
<p>The 26-year-old Dane, a prime candidate to make a Ryder Cup debut this year, shot a three-over-par 75 in the opening round on Thursday after a triple-bogey seven on his last hole, the ninth.</p>
</text>
